WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.302
Email codes: enable, choose and turn off.

2
00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:08.281
Enable optional email verification,
choose the method offered first,

3
00:00:08.281 --> 00:00:11.463
and keep your authenticator available.

4
00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:16.532
First sign in with your
password and authenticator.

5
00:00:16.532 --> 00:00:19.456
Open Sign-in methods from the header.

6
00:00:26.847 --> 00:00:30.064
Your agency decides whether
email codes are allowed.

7
00:00:30.064 --> 00:00:35.723
They need an email address on your account
and are never available to administrators.

8
00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:39.316
Read the warning before
enabling email codes.

9
00:00:39.316 --> 00:00:42.611
Anyone who can read your
email could use them.

10
00:00:42.611 --> 00:00:46.450
Your authenticator stays
required and available.

11
00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:49.757
Enter a current
authenticator code to start.

12
00:00:49.757 --> 00:00:55.164
Confirm that the masked address is yours;
ask your administrator to correct it if

13
00:00:55.164 --> 00:00:56.164
needed.

14
00:00:56.388 --> 00:01:01.698
Read the newest email, enter its
verification code, and choose Confirm and

15
00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:03.133
turn on email codes.

16
00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.972
This proves access to the address.

17
00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:12.024
Under At sign-in, offer first, choose
An email code and save your choice.

18
00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:17.414
This changes the first option,
not the need for a second factor.

19
00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:20.339
Sign out and enter your password again.

20
00:01:20.339 --> 00:01:25.389
Get a code by email is now offered first,
while your authenticator remains an

21
00:01:25.389 --> 00:01:26.789
alternative.

22
00:01:32.316 --> 00:01:34.060
Choose Email me a code.

23
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.761
Enter the code from the newest
email, then Verify and sign in.

24
00:01:38.761 --> 00:01:42.800
Codes work once and expire
after the time shown.

25
00:01:43.162 --> 00:01:47.526
To prefer your authenticator
again, open Sign-in methods,

26
00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:51.753
choose My authenticator
app, and save your choice.

27
00:01:52.106 --> 00:01:55.116
Turn off email codes removes that option.

28
00:01:55.116 --> 00:01:57.391
Your authenticator still works.

29
00:01:57.391 --> 00:02:01.975
Sign in once more to check
that the email option is gone.

30
00:02:11.628 --> 00:02:16.765
In this video you confirmed an email
address with both verification steps,

31
00:02:16.765 --> 00:02:22.527
changed the sign-in method offered first,
and used email verification and turned it

32
00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:23.927
off again.
